 "differences": [
  "Paper Table 1 and the description's participant table differ for some values, so only the values that match within the paper's printed rounding are used as checks. Ages of the bilateral and unilateral groups are about 1 year higher in the description (BV mean 65.4 vs 64.4 printed; UV 64.4 vs 63.4), heights of the bilateral and unilateral groups are about 1 cm higher (BV 1.65 vs 1.64; UV 1.68 vs 1.67), the female counts are 6 (BV), 5 (UV) and 5 (HS) in the description vs 5, 5 and 6 in Table 1, the healthy group's shortest height is 1.62 m vs 1.63 m printed, and its BMI SD and maximum are 3.50 and 29.0 vs 3.6 and 29.1 printed.",
  "The paper's gait-speed table (slow, comfortable, fast) and the GaitSD and anchoring-index results are not reproduced here: the deposit's tasks are the change-of-speed and other trials, not three separate speed blocks, and the authors' gait-cycle processing is not part of the deposit."
